  -- label: band-limited one-sided approximation, exponential tail
  -- claim: $h\text{ continuous},\ |h(u)|\le Me^u,\ h(u)=0\ (u\ge R),\ \varepsilon>0 \Rightarrow \exists g_1\le h\le g_2\text{ band-limited},\ |g_i(u)|\le\frac{C}{1+u^2},\ \int g_1\le\int h\le\int g_2,\ \int g_2-\int g_1\le\varepsilon$
  -- Step functions above and below h on a long interval, Selberg's majorants and minorants of interval indicators,
  -- and a majorant of the exponential tail of small integral.
  have h_bs : ∀ (h : ℝ → ℝ), Continuous h →
